      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IN THE SUMMERTIME NZ (6) was once again right in the mix last time out when runner-up over 2100m at Young, beaten a nose. Beautifully placed and is sure to prove tough to beat again. ALIGHIERI (8) settled in the leading division and finished well to finish second last start over 1770m at Albury, the second minor placing in a row. Has to contend with a very wide draw. Good enough to take out a race like this. DIVA BON VIVA (5) was out of the money two runs ago then broke and finished seventh last start over 2100m at Young, coming home 19 metres from the winner. This doesn't look as hard so she is capable of turning things around. SHADY TREE (9) is heading the right way, improving last time out to finish second at Young over 1720m. Worth consideration.",
